(7593400, 1224649, 31240, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MaryO:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t think I''ve ever photographed one from above. I always go for the side view, for some reason. Maybe ''cuz the curve in the tail makes the bug look very oddly formed from this perspective. But that''s OK; it''s an Assassin Bug, and they''re weird-looking from any angle. Nice macro :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This was taken straight on at him.  Those are his front legs. He would fit on your pinky nail.</td>', 'Originally posted by MaryO: I don''t think I''ve ever photographed one from above. I always go for the side view, for some reason. Maybe ''cuz the curve in the tail makes the bug look very oddly formed from this perspective. But that''s OK; it''s an Assassin Bug, and they''re weird-looking from any angle. Nice macro :-)   This was taken straight on at him.  Those are his front legs. He would fit on your pinky nail.', '2018-08-22 10:08:57.000000', NULL, 0),
